## 5. Data Privacy & Zero-PII Architecture

* **Data Minimization:** Never persist Customer PII (Personally Identifiable Information) such as customer full names, email addresses, phone numbers, or physical delivery addresses in your local/remote database unless explicitly required by the core app function.
* **Audit Identifiers Only:** Store resource IDs (`orderId`, `productId`, `customerId`), numeric values (`totalAmount`), and operational tags/flags (`status`, `appliedTag`).

---

## 6. Database Schema & Prisma Rules

* **Local Database:** Use Neon Postgres only, via `DATABASE_URL` (pooled) and `DIRECT_URL` (unpooled). Do not add a local SQLite database.
* **Portability:** Prefer standard Prisma field types so migrations apply cleanly to Neon Postgres.
* **Standard Audit Log Model Template:**
```prisma
enum ExecutionStatus {
  RECEIVED
  PROCESSING
  SUCCESS
  SKIPPED
  FAILED
}

model OrderAuditLog {
  id            Int             @id @default(autoincrement())
  shop          String
  orderId       String          // e.g. "gid://shopify/Order/12345"
  orderName     String          // e.g. "#1001"
  orderTotal    Float
  appliedTag    String?
  status        ExecutionStatus @default(RECEIVED)
  failureReason String?
  createdAt     DateTime        @default(now())
  updatedAt     DateTime        @updatedAt

  @@unique([shop, orderId])
  @@index([shop, createdAt])
}

```


* Apply schema updates using `npx prisma db push` during prototyping.

