## 7. Frontend UI & Polaris Layout Rules

* **Strict Polaris v12+ Components:**
* DO NOT use deprecated components: `<Stack>`, `<VerticalStack>`, `<HorizontalStack>`.
* ALWAYS use `<BlockStack>` (for vertical layouts) and `<InlineStack>` (for horizontal layouts).
* Use Polaris primitives: `<Page>`, `<Layout>`, `<Layout.Section>`, `<Card>`, `<Text>`, `<Button>`, `<Banner>`, `<TextField>`, `<Checkbox>`.


* **App Bridge v4 Integration:**
* Use App Bridge primitives for page title bars, contextual actions, modals, and toasts.
* Do not build custom floating notification popups when an App Bridge Toast or Polaris Banner is appropriate.


* **Merchant Transparency:**
* Every administrative app must provide an Activity / Audit Log table (`<IndexTable>` or `<DataTable>`) on its settings dashboard showing recent runs, timestamps, and status tags (`SUCCESS`, `SKIPPED`, `FAILED`).
* When empty, always render an `<EmptyState>` guide.



