## 13. Storefront Extensions & Theme Integrity
- **Zero Direct Theme Modifications:** NEVER inject code into `theme.liquid` or use legacy `ScriptTag` APIs.
- **Theme App Extensions Only:** If the app renders any storefront UI (widgets, badges, banners), implement it strictly via Shopify CLI Theme App Extensions (App Embed blocks). When uninstalled, an app must leave zero leftover scripts in the merchant's theme.

---

## 14. Cookie-less Iframe Authentication & Session Tokens
- **Third-Party Cookie Restrictions:** Browsers (Safari, Chrome) block cross-site cookies inside the Shopify Admin iframe.
- **No Cookie Relying Routes:** Never implement custom cookie-based session middleware (e.g., `express-session` or standard HTTP cookies). Rely strictly on App Bridge session tokens (JWT) and `@shopify/shopify-app-remix` token exchange to maintain user state.
- **Content Security Policy (CSP):** Ensure response headers include `frame-ancestors https://[shop].myshopify.com https://admin.shopify.com` to prevent clickjacking while allowing Shopify to embed the app.

---

## 15. In-App Navigation & App Bridge Primitives
- **Internal Navigation:** Do NOT use native `<a href="...">` tags or `window.location.href` for navigation within the Shopify admin. Use Remix `<Link>` or Polaris navigation hooks to preserve the App Bridge session context without reloading the parent iframe.
- **Title Bar & Action Buttons:** Use the `<ui-title-bar>` web component (or App Bridge `TitleBar`) for the top action buttons (e.g., "Save", "Settings") rather than floating custom headers.
- **Support & Feedback Channel:** Every embedded app must include a visible link or button for merchant support (e.g., mailto or contact modal) accessible directly inside the UI.

---

## 16. API Versioning Standard
- Never hardcode deprecated or arbitrary API version strings.
- Always import and reference `LATEST_API_VERSION` from `@shopify/shopify-api` in `shopify.server.ts` to ensure the app stays on supported quarterly release cycles.

